---
import Layout from "#/ui/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Seccy — Hardware-backed keys, everyday tools"
  description="SSH, Git signing, and encrypted secrets. Secure Enclave on macOS. TPM and FIDO2 on Linux."
>
  <div class="page">
    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <img src="/icon.png" width="96" height="96" alt="" />
        <h1>Seccy</h1>
        <h2>Your keys. Your hardware. Your say.</h2>
        <p>
          SSH authentication, Git signing, and encrypted secrets with
          hardware-backed keys and authorization you can see.
        </p>
        <nav>
          <a class="link" href="#install">Install Seccy →</a><a
            class="link"
            href="https://github.com/kossnocorp/seccy">GitHub ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </section>
      <section class="details">
        <h2>One agent. The tools you already use.</h2>
        <dl>
          <dt>macOS: Secure Enclave + Touch ID</dt>
          <dd>
            Non-exportable P-256 keys, with biometric approval for prompt keys.
            Distributed as a signed, notarized app bundle.
          </dd>
          <dt>Linux: TPM + FIDO2</dt>
          <dd>
            TPM-generated keys protected by your security key, with GNOME
            prompts and Secret Service integration.
          </dd>
          <dt>SSH, Git, and fnox</dt>
          <dd>
            Use the standard SSH agent protocol, sign commits, sync public keys
            to GitHub, and encrypt secrets through the included fnox provider.
          </dd>
          <dt>Know what is asking</dt>
          <dd>
            Inspect local client details, key identities, and operation logs.
            Script everything with JSON and built-in jq queries.
          </dd>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <section id="install" class="details">
        <h2>Get started</h2>
        <p>
          Run in your logged-in desktop session. The installer downloads the
          matching release, verifies its checksum, installs the complete
          package, and walks through key and agent setup.
        </p>
        <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://seccy.fyi/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
        <p>
          macOS requires a Secure Enclave-equipped Mac. Linux requires GNOME, a
          TPM 2.0 device, and a compatible FIDO2 authenticator. Linux setup uses
          sudo to install the TPM system service.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="link" href="https://github.com/kossnocorp/seccy/releases"
            >Release archives</a
          > · <a class="link" href="https://github.com/kossnocorp/seccy#readme"
            >Documentation</a
          > · <a
            class="link"
            href="https://github.com/kossnocorp/seccy/blob/main/docs/linux/README.md"
            >Linux requirements</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer>
      Sasha Koss © 2026 · <a
        class="link"
        href="https://github.com/kossnocorp/seccy">Open source</a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  @reference "#/ui/styles/global.css";
  .page {
    @apply w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 sm:px-12 sm:py-20;
  }
  main {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-16;
  }
  section {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-5 max-w-2xl;
  }
  h1 {
    @apply text-5xl sm:text-7xl font-bold text-(--color-heading-1);
  }
  h2 {
    @apply text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold text-(--color-heading-2);
  }
  p,
  dd {
    @apply text-lg text-(--color-text);
  }
  nav {
    @apply flex gap-6;
  }
  dt {
    @apply font-semibold mt-6 mb-2;
  }
  pre {
    @apply overflow-x-auto p-5 rounded-lg border border-(--color-code-border) bg-(--color-code-canvas) text-(--color-code-ink) text-sm;
  }
  footer {
    @apply mt-20 text-sm opacity-70;
  }
</style>
